RV32I Level 3 load/store subsystem test
=======================================

Memory image: tb/mem/load_store_subsystem_test.mem
Each line is one 32-bit instruction, beginning at byte address 0.

Coverage:
  - LB/LBU from all four byte lanes, including sign and zero extension.
  - LH/LHU from both aligned halfword lanes, including sign and zero extension.
  - SB to all four byte lanes; immediate loads check each stored byte.
  - SH to low/high halfword lanes; immediate signed/unsigned loads check data.
  - LW/SW at multiple word addresses, checking lane preservation and address decode.
  - Every load is immediately followed by an ADDI that consumes its result. This
    exercises the synchronous memory response and load-use stall/forwarding path.

The program branches to FAIL on any mismatch. At completion:
  dmem[128] = 0x00000055 : all checks passed
  dmem[128] = 0x000000EE : a check failed
The signature is stored at byte address 0x200.

Seed word at byte address 0x100:
  0x80FF8001, bytes at increasing addresses: 01, 80, FF, 80.
SB test word at byte address 0x104 should finish as 0x44332211.
SH test word at byte address 0x108 should finish as 0x04560123.
Additional SW/LW test word at byte address 0x110 should be 0x89ABC123.

